  "description": "Reid Bikes H24 | 24 inch kids' bike\nLightweight design for big adventures - the perfect 24\" kids' bike for 8-11 year olds who love exploring.Weighing just 8.3kg, this Reid Bikes H24, 24\" kids' bike stands out for its easy handling and nimble feel, helping young riders gain confidence and enjoy every ride. The low weight makes climbing, turning, and controlling the bike smoother and more natural, especially at this price point.Part of the Reid Bikes H Series kids' bike range, the H24 children's bike is constructed from durable yet lightweight 6061 aluminium alloy, the frame and fork deliver strength without excess bulk. Equipped with a 7-speed Shimano drivetrain and a 14-28T cassette, it lets kids easily shift gears and take on varied terrain with confidence.Jak V-brakes provide reliable stopping power, with alloy brake levers sized for smaller hands to ensure comfort and control. The 24 x 1.5\" Vee tires offer excellent grip across different surfaces, while the junior-sized saddle, riser handlebars, and ergonomic grips make for a comfortable ride.Perfect for riders ready to take their skills further, this lightweight 24\" kids' bike combines performance, versatility, and ease-of-use in a smart, kid-friendly package.\nWho is the Reid Bikes H24 for?\nThe H24 kids' bike is ideal for:\n\n8–11 year olds ready to take their riding further\n\nGrowing riders developing greater confidence and control on two wheels\n\nChildren moving up from a 20\" kids' bike and ready for a larger bike\n\nYoung riders exploring more varied terrain, from parks and bike paths to local trails\n\nKids ready to make the most of gears, with 7 speeds to help tackle hills and changing terrain\n\nRiders who want a lightweight, responsive bike that’s easy to handle on longer adventures\n\nParents looking for a durable, versatile bike that can keep up as their child’s riding skills develop\n\nFind the right fit\nChoosing the right bike size helps your child ride comfortably, confidently and safely. Use our Kids' Bike Size Guide by clicking the tab above to find the right Reid bike based on your child’s height and age.",
